Filter the client IP under every proxy's own header name, not just
``X-Forwarded-For``. ``SENSITIVE_HEADERS`` listed ``X-Forwarded-For`` and
``X-Real-Ip``, so behind a proxy that names its own header -- Fly.io's
``Fly-Client-Ip``, Cloudflare's ``CF-Connecting-IP``, Akamai's
``True-Client-Ip`` -- the visitor's real address was sent to Sentry verbatim,
directly beside a ``[Filtered]`` ``X-Forwarded-For`` in the same event, while
``should_send_pii()`` was closed. An IP address is identifying data, and the
point of that default is that an operator who has configured nothing does not
ship it. Found in production on Fly; pre-existing, not a sentry-sdk 3
regression.

Entries must be spelled as the ``key[5:].replace("_", "-").title()`` transform
produces them (``Cf-Connecting-Ip``, not the vendor's ``CF-Connecting-IP``), or
they can never match while still looking correct, so a new test asserts every
name in the set round trips through that transform.
